ially at a time of rising prices  not only is it suggesting that poorer  families ordinary folk can't look after  themselves but it's also going to be  dipping into their own pockets at the  time when there's a cost of living  crisis and so i think what the  government should be doing instead is  letting families making make their own  decisions when it comes to what they  consume and what they buy for themselves  labour say political problems for the  prime minister have led to a  watered-down strategy i think if  actually this had been produced a few  months ago it would have been a much  stronger policy but the prime minister  is no longer capable of leading his own  party let alone the country and of  course we're all losers as a consequence  of that so this is going to have to be  revisited it is astonishing that our  country doesn't have a proper food plan  a frequent jogger boris johnson said his  brush with covid made him determined to  help people lose weight and improve  their health but set against a tricky  political backdrop doing that may prove  more a marathon than a sprint rob powell  sky news in westminster
 

